<title>UK: Czarnikow sees higher EU 1996/97 sugar output.</title>
<headline>Czarnikow sees higher EU 1996/97 sugar output.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar production in the European Union (EU) should reach 17.93 million tonnes raw value in 1996/97, 906,000 more than in the previous season, Czarnikow Sugar said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The EU produced 17.03 million tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Czarnikow's latest estimate was just 36,000 tonnes higher than its last figure released in February.</p>
<p>It cited further minor late improvements in the west of the continent as EU producers finally assessed their crops.</p>
<p>France, the region's largest producer, was expected to turn out 4.59 million tonnes after 4.60 million in 1995/96, while Germany's output was pegged at 4.55 million after a previous 4.16 million.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
